        "headline": "The 40/60 Principle",
        "body": "An asymmetric layout deliberately avoids equal columns. The smaller side (40%) acts as an anchor — holding navigation, context, or key visuals — while the larger side (60%) carries the main content. The sticky sidebar stays visible as users scroll through content, creating a grounded editorial experience. This pattern is widely used in photography portfolios, editorial lookbooks, and modern contact pages where visual hierarchy matters more than content density.",
